==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uber Clearance|1}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
*3 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*4 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Boraphim]] spawns as the boss after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Professor A.]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Capy|Capies]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[H. Nah]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Welcome to the "new" Otherworld Colosseum, where this time the Colosseum Rule is one that solely benefits Ubers, just like Plus One: Uber. Because of this rule, the cost to deploy Ubers is comically low, with heavyweights like [[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Dioramos]] now costing 330¢ and lightweights like first form and ultra form [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]] costing 38¢! Obviously, because you can now deploy an Uber early to sweep the whole stage, this whole Colosseum is designed around pressuring you hard and fast by spawning boss enemies incredibly quickly. While it's not as hard to do Uberless as Plus One: Uber, do expect an uphill battle.

For example, after only 23 seconds a Boraphim spawns, with barely anything spawning to supply you with cash. Because of this, it is vital to farm the Mr. Angels or Jackrabbit with someone who can Double Bounty these peons to get as much as cash as needed to fight off the Boraphim. A high-levelled [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] should be enough to stall Boraphim while he's mostly alone, while you stack DPS on him using units like [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. By the time the Capy and the Professor A. start approaching you, the Boraphim should be long dead. While this might seem pretty tedious to take care of given your limited line, it's nothing that a Thunderbolt and a well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can't take care of. From there, you can use methods of chip like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]'s Waves, Courier, or simply just running [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] to chip Profesor A. down. If you take too long to beat the stage, the stage will spawn H. Nahs and Teacher Bears, but you can beat H. Nah to death with a bunch of Courier hits, and Teacher Bear goes down to a few of Slime's Waves fairly easily.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Ubers to beat up Professor A. are pretty good here to allow you to beat the stage quickly and not have to worry about the H. Nah. Examples include generalist backliners, [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Daliasan]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]], or just anti-Red specialists like [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]] and [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]].

